Package: MuTATE
Title: Multi-Target Automated Tree Engine (MuTATE)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sarah", "Ayton", , "sarah.ayton@columbia.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5247-9912")) )
Description: Provides functions to recursively partition a dataset on binary
    feature splits chosen jointly across multiple outcome variables of
    different types (categorical, continuous, count, and survival), rather
    than a single target as in a standard decision tree. This produces one
    interpretable tree that characterizes candidate subgroups across several
    outcomes of interest simultaneously, while retaining model
    interpretability. The package includes model fitting, pruning,
    cross-validated hyperparameter tuning, prediction on new data, and
    visualization functions.
